                    "id": "complaints.md#s1",
                    "doc": "complaints.md",
                    "score": 1.591,
                    "text": "Complaints\n## Difference from a dispute\nA dispute concerns a specific transaction. A complaint concerns the service\nitself: a delay, an error, or the conduct of an agent. The two follow separate\nprocesses."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "disputes-process.md#s1",
                    "doc": "disputes-process.md",
                    "score": 1.2857,
                    "text": "Dispute handling process\n## Raising a dispute\nA dispute is raised against a single settled transaction. The customer supplies\nthe transaction reference and a reason code. The agent verifies eligibility\nbefore the case is opened; an ineligible request is refused with the failing\ncondition named, except where confidentiality rules apply."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "disputes-process.md#s6",
                    "doc": "disputes-process.md",
                    "score": 1.2374,
                    "text": "Dispute handling process\n## Withdrawing a dispute\nA customer may withdraw a dispute at any time before resolution. Withdrawal is\nfinal; the same transaction cannot be disputed again under the same reason code."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "glossary.md#s7",
                    "doc": "glossary.md",
                    "score": 1.1785,
                    "text": "Glossary\n## Provisional credit\nA temporary refund applied while a dispute is reviewed; reversed if the dispute\nis declined."
                  }
                ]
              },
